{
  "protocol_version": "1",
  "comment": [
    "The canonical set of machine operations, and how each one is reached over",
    "HTTP through the Yon host in server/ (docs/YON.md, ADR 0007).",
    "",
    "This file is asserted by test/contract against the engine's own dispatch",
    "table (parsed from the processor, so the manifest cannot claim an operation",
    "the engine does not route), against the protocol README (so no operation",
    "ships undocumented), and against the Yon controllers in server/controllers",
    "(so a route cannot appear, move or disappear without saying so here).",
    "",
    "http_coverage gives every operation exactly one category:",
    "  routed: the listed RPC routes call it (some operations have a self-service",
    "    and an administrator route);",
    "  standard_endpoint: served only by the listed standard protocol routes",
    "    through standards.dispatch, named by the host-adapter endpoint;",
    "  command_line_only: never routed; it needs local operator access;",
    "  not_routed_for_security: never routed; its result is host-only material.",
    "",
    "Every operation is also reachable without HTTP through the machine protocol",
    "(`sesame exec --loop`, api/machine/v1) and the Go package in server/packages."
  ],
